# *** THIS FIXTURE IS DERIVED, NOT OBSERVED. ***
#
# EXPECTED VERDICT: NOT-MEASURED.
# It is `pass-observed-no-net-section` with ONE LINE DELETED: the
# `   LVS REPORT MAXIMUM                     1000` line out of its LVS
# PARAMETERS block. Nothing else differs, and no line is edited.
#
# WHAT IT PROVES: an UNSTATED cap is not an ABSENT cap. Control N7 declares
# the discrepancy list saturated when the parsed count reaches
# `LVS REPORT MAXIMUM`; with no cap parsed, N7 cannot be evaluated at all, and
# a control that could not run must not be reported as a control that passed.
#
# THIS ARM IS ALSO THE DISCRIMINATOR FOR `ALL`. Until 2026-08-27 the parser
# required `(\d+)`, so the 13 runs on this site whose deck emits
# `LVS REPORT MAXIMUM  ALL` left `report_maximum` at None -- the SAME state as
# this fixture, in which the line is genuinely gone. The two are now distinct:
# `ALL` is a MEASURED statement that the tool truncated nothing, and only a
# genuinely absent line trips N11. Mutation M15 takes `ALL` back out of the
# pattern, at which point the three `ALL` arms
# (pass-observed-vacuous-pairing, fail-vacuous-but-layout-is-a-path,
# not-measured-vacuous-flood) start tripping N11 and catch it.
#
# derived from: ci/fixtures/lvs-missing-connection/pass-observed-no-net-section
#               (itself an EXTRACT of lvs_run_nopadbox; see PROVENANCE.md)
#



